WEBVTT

00:21:57.814 --> 00:22:00.045
I'm going to end up
favoring the algorithm.

00:22:00.069 --> 00:22:02.817
AG: Cade Massey is an expert
on decision making.

00:22:02.841 --> 00:22:04.692
We codirect Wharton People Analytics

00:22:04.716 --> 00:22:07.945
where we use data to improve
how people work and lead.

00:22:07.969 --> 00:22:11.036
One of our big projects
is about assessing character strengths,

00:22:11.060 --> 00:22:13.465
which is fun, since Cade
and I have similar values,

00:22:13.489 --> 00:22:14.972
but different worldviews.

00:22:15.499 --> 00:22:19.435
Cade and I have found ourselves
disagreeing on artificial intelligence.

00:22:19.459 --> 00:22:22.535
Many companies are using AI
to help narrow down candidates,

00:22:22.559 --> 00:22:24.472
looking for certain keywords in resumes,

00:22:24.496 --> 00:22:28.141
or even scanning people's faces
in video interviews.

00:22:28.165 --> 00:22:31.102
Some people think this practice
is smart and efficient,